import re

SOURCE='https://tbdskillteambattlereports.wordpress.com/2024/08/01/my-first-kill-team-game/'

def revise(html,photo):
    html=html.replace('<a href="#gallery">Photographs</a>','<a href="#results">Results</a><a href="#gallery">Photographs</a>')
    html=html.replace('<small>MISSION FOCUS</small>The installation’s archives','<small>MISSION</small>Loot and Salvage · Open Play')
    html=html.replace('A photographic narrative reconstruction. Sections follow areas of action rather than verified turns; connecting prose is dramatised. No final score or winner is recorded in the available account.',f'Campaign framing meets the recorded game: the four turning points and result follow <a href="{SOURCE}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the original battle report, published 1 August 2024</a>. Ghost Talon and T-601’s mission provide the narrative setting; the tabletop mission was Loot and Salvage.')
    html=html.replace('A small force with ground to cover: the bunkers, the open approach and the tower overlooking the central installation.','Hunter Cadre: two fire teams of three stealth suits. Five carry burst cannons; one carries a fusion blaster. Mobility and concealment will have to make up for their fewer activations.')
    html=html.replace('Five Warriors and four Immortals. Their presence across the central roof and bunker positions puts the T’au approach under pressure.','Tomb World: five Warriors with gauss flayers; three Immortals with gauss blasters, including the leader; and one Immortal with a tesla carbine. Nine activations put pressure on the six-suit cadre.')
    engagement='''<section id="engagement"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE ENGAGEMENT</p><h2>Four turning points.<br>No room for a wasted move.</h2><p>Loot and Salvage sets six objectives across the listening post. Both players choose Recon; the Tomb World force deploys first, and wins the initiative roll that opens the game.</p></div>
<div class="opening">'''+photo(1,'Deployment at Kappa-9: six objectives, the central landing pad, two bunkers and the Vox tower.')+'''<div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">DEPLOYMENT / LOOT AND SALVAGE</p><h3>The race for the station</h3><p>The Necrons deploy mostly with Engage orders, concealing the operatives at the front of the advance. Ghost Talon answers with the reverse: most suits begin concealed, while those nearest the objectives prepare to act openly.</p><p>Every marker offers a reason to leave cover. The Vox tower holds objective six; the central landing pad overlooks objective four. The two bunker roofs will become the site of an expensive opening exchange.</p><p>In the campaign, this is the struggle for access to Kappa-9’s records. On the tabletop, the task is more immediate: secure objectives, preserve the operatives who can reach them, and keep scoring.</p></div></div>
<nav class="turn-nav" aria-label="Turning points"><a href="#turn-1">01 / First contact</a><a href="#turn-2">02 / Withdrawal</a><a href="#turn-3">03 / Repositioning</a><a href="#turn-4">04 / Last chances</a></nav>
<div class="chapter" id="turn-1"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">TURNING POINT 01 / INITIATIVE: NECRONS</p><span class="chapter-no">I</span><h3>A costly opening</h3><p>T-601’s force secures objectives one and four. Ghost Talon answers at two and six, a stealth suit flying onto the Vox tower to claim its elevated position.</p><p>A Warrior moves onto the bunker roof, threatening objective five. A burst-cannon suit opens fire and leaves it with three wounds. Another Warrior retaliates, reducing the exposed attacker to four wounds. Ghost Talon commits a second suit and brings the first Warrior down; the Necrons invoke Reanimation Protocols.</p><p>The commitment leaves both suits exposed. A gauss-blaster Immortal moves into position and takes one out of action. Another Immortal fires on the remaining rooftop suit, which ends the exchange on four wounds.</p><p>Near the tower, T’au reinforcements wound an advancing Warrior, but subsequent overwatch fire misses. The Necrons continue moving toward the tower and objective three. Ghost Talon has disrupted the push for five, at the cost of one suit and a second left in danger.</p></div>'''+photo(4,'Turning point one: the T’au hold the tower and approach objectives while Necrons occupy the central landing pad.')+'''</div><div class="photo-pair landscape">'''+photo(3,'Turning point one: one stealth suit is down on the bunker roof, and the other remains exposed to Necron fire.')+photo(2,'Turning point one: Necrons establish firing positions across the landing pad and around the Vox tower.')+'''</div>
<div class="chapter reverse" id="turn-2"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">TURNING POINT 02 / INITIATIVE: NECRONS</p><span class="chapter-no">II</span><h3>Live to score again</h3><p>The downed Warrior fails its reanimation roll. Living Metal restores wounds to the damaged Necrons, and the Warrior at objective four opens the firefight with a devastating volley: three critical hits and one normal hit finish the surviving rooftop stealth suit.</p><p>Two suits lost. Ghost Talon changes its priorities. The tower operative conceals, secures objective six and begins withdrawing toward the surviving team. At objective two, another suit scores before falling back toward the barracks. The T’au leader takes a chance and secures objective three.</p><p>The Necrons keep building pressure. A Warrior claims objective five; another scores at one and advances toward two. The Immortal leader closes on the T’au commander, while a Warrior and Immortal head toward the tower.</p><p>With the surviving suits concealed or withdrawing, the later Necron activations find no legal shots. T-601’s numerical advantage buys ground, but Ghost Talon keeps its remaining operatives moving.</p></div>'''+photo(7,'Turning point two: Ghost Talon pulls back from the centre while Necrons spread toward the remaining objectives.')+'''</div><div class="photo-pair landscape">'''+photo(5,'Turning point two: both stealth suits on the bunker roof are now out of action.')+photo(8,'Turning point two: Necrons retain their central positions as Ghost Talon shifts toward the barracks.')+'''</div>
<div class="chapter" id="turn-3"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">TURNING POINT 03 / INITIATIVE: T’AU</p><span class="chapter-no">III</span><h3>Back to the tower</h3><p>Ghost Talon wins initiative. The damaged Necron force benefits from Living Metal again, but the fallen Warrior still fails to reanimate. The T’au commander sends the former tower occupant back to objective six: concealed on that platform, it has a position the Necrons cannot readily shoot or charge.</p><p>The Immortal leader claims objective three, forcing the T’au leader away. Ghost Talon’s operative at two secures the marker and retreats toward the table edge. The leader escapes onto a bunker roof, beyond the Immortal’s charge range.</p><p>The fusion-blaster suit joins the leader on the roof, setting up an attack on objective five in the next turning point. Across the station, Warriors score again at four and five.</p><p>Necron reinforcements reach the tower ladder but have no legal target above them. Two Immortals advance toward objective two, while the Warrior that had pushed away from one returns to guard it. Both teams are arranging their last scoring opportunities.</p></div>'''+photo(9,'Turning point three: the concealed T’au tower operative is back above Necron infantry gathered at the base.')+'''</div><div class="photo-pair landscape">'''+photo(10,'Turning point three: an overhead view of the repositioned forces before the final push.')+photo(11,'Turning point three: Necrons hold the opposite bunker while the surviving T’au prepare their last-turn attack.')+'''</div>
<div class="chapter reverse" id="turn-4"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">TURNING POINT 04 / INITIATIVE: T’AU</p><span class="chapter-no">IV</span><h3>Everything left to play for</h3><p>Ghost Talon keeps initiative. The fusion-blaster suit changes to Engage, destroys the Warrior on the opposite bunker roof and flies across to its victim’s position. The Warrior at objective four answers: it secures the marker, turns and shoots the fusion suit out of action.</p><p>A wounded stealth suit then slips in to steal objective two. An Immortal charges in retaliation, but fails to kill it. Up on the Vox tower, Ghost Talon’s operative switches to Engage, secures objective six and destroys the tesla-carbine Immortal.</p><p>The Necrons try to silence the tower. A gauss-blaster Immortal moves for a shot and misses. The T’au leader flies across to secure objective five. A Warrior also fires at the tower suit and misses; overwatch from above destroys another Immortal.</p><p>The Necron Warrior at objective one stays concealed and secures its marker. After four turning points, both forces have extracted the same value from the field: ten victory points apiece.</p></div>'''+photo(14,'Turning point four: the final contests for the bunkers and objectives, with T’au and Necron models at close quarters.')+'''</div><div class="photo-pair landscape">'''+photo(12,'Turning point four: the tower operative survives the incoming fire; the Warrior at objective four remains on the landing pad.')+photo(13,'Turning point four: the bunker fighting after the fusion-blaster strike and Necron retaliation.')+'''</div></section>'''
    html=re.sub(r'<section id="engagement">.*?</section>',lambda _:engagement,html,count=1,flags=re.S)
    results='''<section id="results"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / THE RESULT</p><h2>A draw, earned the hard way.</h2><p>Neither force breaks the deadlock. Ghost Talon’s late objective grabs and tower fire keep the game level despite the early losses.</p></div><div class="scoreboard" aria-label="Final result: Hunter Cadre 10, Tomb World 10, draw"><div><small>HUNTER CADRE / GHOST TALON</small><strong>10</strong><span>VICTORY POINTS</span></div><p>DRAW</p><div><small>TOMB WORLD / T-601</small><strong>10</strong><span>VICTORY POINTS</span></div></div>
<div class="mvp-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">NECRON MVP / OBJECTIVE FOUR</p><h3>The landing-pad sentinel</h3><p>The Warrior at objective four secures it every turning point and destroys two stealth suits, including the fusion-blaster operative in the final exchange. A single dependable scoring position anchors the Necron result.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">T’AU MVP / OBJECTIVE SIX</p><h3>The suit on the Vox tower</h3><p>The tower operative denies the Necrons access to objective six for much of the game. Its final-turn burst cannon and overwatch destroy two Immortals at a crucial moment, helping turn survival into a draw.</p></div></div>
<details class="debrief"><summary>From the tabletop · lessons from a first game</summary><div class="prose"><p>The original account describes an enjoyable but lengthy first game, with frequent rule lookups and mistakes that were walked back. Losing two suits early made the difference in available activations especially painful; concealment, movement and objective play became essential to the T’au recovery.</p><p><strong>A rules mistake shaped the game.</strong> The author notes that Implacable March was misplayed: affected Necrons were allowed to secure objectives and Dash when they should not have been. The report records its use each turning point. This account preserves the game as played and its recorded 10–10 result, without attempting to calculate a corrected score.</p></div></details></section>'''
    html=html.replace('<section class="aftermath">',results+'<section class="aftermath">')
    html=html.replace('03 / BEYOND THE FIREFIGHT','04 / BEYOND THE FIREFIGHT').replace('04 / PHOTOGRAPHIC RECORD','05 / PHOTOGRAPHIC RECORD')
    html=html.replace('<div class="record"><span class="status-dot"></span><div><strong>Outcome: unconfirmed</strong><p>The available record contains no verified score, winner or complete casualty tally.</p></div></div>','<div class="record"><span class="status-dot"></span><div><strong>Kappa-9: contested</strong><p>The tabletop engagement ends in a draw. Whether either side uncovers the listening post’s deeper secrets remains a question for the campaign.</p></div></div>')
    html=re.sub(r'<div class="gallery">.*?</div></section>',lambda _:'<div class="gallery">'+photo(15,'The Necron MVP: the Warrior beside objective four, which scored every turning point and destroyed two stealth suits.')+photo(16,'An additional overhead view of the tower, landing pad and bunker approaches.')+'</div></section>',html,count=1,flags=re.S)
    html=html.replace('<footer><p class="eyebrow">',f'<footer><p class="source-credit">Game record: <a href="{SOURCE}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My first kill team game!</a> · TBDs Kill team battle reports · 1 August 2024. Campaign framing adapted from our Kappa-9 discussion.</p><p class="eyebrow">')
    return html
